{{!
    @template enrol_apply/review

    One enrolment application, with the controls to decide it.

    The POST this form makes is the same one the queue makes, which is why manage.php's
    handler needs no branch of its own: a formaction naming the decision, a non-empty
    userenrolments array, and the session key. The applicant id travels in a hidden input
    rather than a checkbox because there is only ever one of them here, and each decision is
    a submit button carrying its own formaction value, so the button that was pressed is the
    decision that is taken.

    Every value this template renders ITSELF is the PLAIN spelling and is output through a
    double stash, which escapes each exactly once - the course name included, for which the
    renderer asks for the plain spelling explicitly because format_string()'s escape flag
    defaults to true. The exceptions are deliberate and flagged where they sit:
    the comment, which arrives already escaped from format_text(FORMAT_PLAIN) so that the line
    breaks the applicant typed survive, and the role names inside the partial this template
    includes, which core's own element-select.mustache also triple stashes.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * formurl string - url the decision form posts back to
    * sesskey string - session key guarding the state change
    * userenrolmentid int - the application being decided
    * courselabel string - label of the course row
    * coursename string - full name of the course applied for, plain spelling
    * courseurl string - link to the course
    * hasidentity boolean - whether this reader may see any identifying detail of the applicant
    * identity array - one entry per identity field the site named and this reader may see, each
      carrying a label and a value, both in the PLAIN spelling. They are labelled because they
      run together on one line and several are opaque without one. There is no e-mail row of its
      own any more:
      the address is one of these when showuseridentity names it and absent when it does not,
      which is what stops this panel and the snapshot below it disagreeing about the same reader
    * profileurl string - the applicant's profile in this course
    * profilelabel string - text of the profile link
    * hascapacity boolean - whether this reader may see the method's own limits and counts. A
      mentor reaches this page through the applicant's user context and holds nothing in the
      course, so they are shown the course but not its enrolment numbers - the same line the
      group and role choosers draw
    * capacitylabel string - heading of the panel saying where the application lands
    * placeslabel string - label of the places row
    * places string - places taken against the limit, already formatted, or the no-limit wording
    * applicantslabel string - label of the applicants row
    * applicants string - applications held against the limit, or the no-limit wording
    * deferredlabel string - label of the deferred row
    * deferred string - how many of those applications are deferred. A bare count and not "n of
      m": it is a subset of the applicants row rather than a limit of its own, and it is here
      because nothing ever frees a deferred row from the applicant cap
    * hasdecision boolean - whether a colleague has already decided this one, which today means
      it was deferred; a pending application has no decision to describe, and the page is not
      reachable at all for the other two states
    * decisionlabel string - heading of that panel
    * decision string - who deferred it and when, plain spelling
    * hasdecisionmessage boolean - whether they wrote anything to the applicant
    * decisionmessage string - what they wrote, ALREADY escaped with its line breaks converted,
      which is why it is triple stashed
    * hasdecisionnote boolean - whether they left a note for whoever reads this next
    * decisionnotelabel string - label of that note
    * decisionnote string - the note, ALREADY escaped with its line breaks converted, hence the
      triple stash. It is shown here and deliberately NOT pre-filled into the note box below,
      because that writer clears on empty and a pre-filled box would carry one decision's reason
      into the next
    * hashistory boolean - whether this reader may see earlier applications AND there are any
    * historylabel string - heading of the earlier-applications list
    * history array - one entry per earlier application, each with the date it was submitted and
      the outcome as the report's own formatter words it
    * appliedlabel string - label of the application date row
    * applied string - when the application was submitted, already formatted
    * statuslabel string - label of the state row
    * status string - whether the application is pending or on the waiting list
    * commentlabel string - label of the applicant's comment
    * hascomment boolean - whether the applicant wrote one
    * comment string - what the applicant wrote, ALREADY escaped and with its line breaks
      converted by format_text(FORMAT_PLAIN), which is why it is triple stashed
    * nocomment string - what to say when they wrote nothing
    * hassnapshot boolean - whether the applicant submitted any profile detail this reader may see
    * snapshotlabel string - heading of the submitted-details list
    * snapshot array - one entry per submitted field the reader may see, each with the label and
      the value as they were submitted, both the PLAIN spelling and output through double
      stashes. A value can hold newlines, because a textarea custom field is offerable, so the
      cell carries the same white-space rule the report's own free-text cells do rather than
      converting them to markup
    * everything enrol_apply/decision_controls requires
    * stickyfooter string - the three decisions, already rendered into a core sticky footer by
      the renderer and interpolated INSIDE this form. The footer is never moved in the DOM -
      its placement is CSS - so the submits inside it post with the rest of the form, exactly as
      the queue's own bar does

    Example context (json):
    {
        "formurl": "https://example.com/enrol/apply/manage.php?userenrol=42",
        "sesskey": "Ab12Cd34Ef",
        "userenrolmentid": 42,
        "courselabel": "Course",
        "coursename": "R&D < Team induction",
        "courseurl": "https://example.com/course/view.php?id=7",
        "hasidentity": true,
        "identity": [
            {"label": "Username", "value": "jsa"},
            {"label": "ID number", "value": "2026-0071"}
        ],
        "profileurl": "https://example.com/user/view.php?id=5&course=7",
        "profilelabel": "View profile",
        "hascapacity": true,
        "capacitylabel": "Where this lands",
        "placeslabel": "Places",
        "places": "8 of 20",
        "applicantslabel": "Maximum applicants",
        "applicants": "35 of 40",
        "deferredlabel": "Deferred",
        "deferred": "12",
        "hasdecision": true,
        "decisionlabel": "The decision so far",
        "decision": "Deferred by Ana Souza on 10/08/26, 14:02.",
        "hasdecisionmessage": true,
        "decisionmessage": "Waiting for the second group to open.",
        "hasdecisionnote": true,
        "decisionnotelabel": "Note for the record",
        "decisionnote": "Second intake opens in September; hold until the registrar confirms.",
        "hashistory": true,
        "historylabel": "Earlier applications to this course",
        "history": [
            {"applied": "04/06/26, 11:02", "outcome": "Cancelled"}
        ],
        "appliedlabel": "Application date",
        "applied": "25/08/26, 09:14",
        "statuslabel": "Status",
        "status": "Awaiting a decision",
        "commentlabel": "Comment",
        "hascomment": true,
        "comment": "I would like to join this course.",
        "nocomment": "The applicant did not write anything.",
        "hassnapshot": true,
        "snapshotlabel": "Details submitted with this application",
        "snapshot": [
            {"label": "City/town", "value": "Ouro Preto"},
            {"label": "Registration number", "value": "2026-0042"}
        ],
        "hasgroups": true,
        "grouplabel": "Groups to join on approval",
        "grouphelp": "Leave empty to use the groups configured on the enrolment method.",
        "groups": [
            {"id": 3, "name": "Tutorial A"}
        ],
        "hasroles": true,
        "rolelabel": "Role to assign on approval",
        "rolehelp": "Leave it alone to use the role configured on the enrolment method.",
        "roledefault": "Use the enrolment method's role",
        "roles": [
            {"id": 5, "name": "Student"}
        ],
        "messagelabel": "Message to the applicant",
        "messagehelp": "Included in the message they receive. Optional.",
        "messagevalue": "",
        "notelabel": "Note for the record",
        "notehelp": "Kept with the application for whoever looks at it next. The applicant never sees it.",
        "notevalue": "",
        "stickyfooter": "<div id=\"sticky-footer\"><button type=\"submit\">Confirm</button></div>"
    }
}}
<form id="enrol_apply_review_form" class="enrol_apply-review" method="post" action="{{formurl}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
    <input type="hidden" name="userenrolments[]" value="{{userenrolmentid}}">
    <div class="enrol_apply-applicant d-flex flex-wrap align-items-start gap-2 mb-3">
        <div class="flex-grow-1">
            {{#hasidentity}}
                <dl class="enrol_apply-identity small text-muted mb-1 d-flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                    {{#identity}}
                        <div><dt class="d-inline fw-normal">{{label}}:</dt>
                            <dd class="d-inline ms-1">{{value}}</dd></div>
                    {{/identity}}
                </dl>
            {{/hasidentity}}
            <p class="mb-0">{{statuslabel}}: <strong>{{status}}</strong>
                <span class="text-muted">&middot; {{appliedlabel}} {{applied}}</span></p>
        </div>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm" href="{{profileurl}}">{{profilelabel}}</a>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-lg-7">
            {{#hasdecision}}
                <div class="alert alert-info" role="status">
                    <strong>{{decisionlabel}}</strong> {{decision}}
                    {{#hasdecisionmessage}}<div class="mt-1">{{{decisionmessage}}}</div>{{/hasdecisionmessage}}
                    {{#hasdecisionnote}}
                        <div class="mt-1"><strong>{{decisionnotelabel}}:</strong> {{{decisionnote}}}</div>
                    {{/hasdecisionnote}}
                </div>
            {{/hasdecision}}
            <h2 class="h5">{{commentlabel}}</h2>
            <div class="mb-3">
                {{#hascomment}}{{{comment}}}{{/hascomment}}
                {{^hascomment}}<span class="text-muted">{{nocomment}}</span>{{/hascomment}}
            </div>
            {{#hassnapshot}}
                {{!
                    The wrapper is load bearing, not decoration: renderer_test scopes its
                    live-profile assertions to this class, because the page legitimately shows
                    identifying values elsewhere and a whole-page assertion would either fail for
                    an unrelated reason or pass while holding the wrong thing.
                }}
                <div class="enrol_apply-snapshot">
                    <h2 class="h5">{{snapshotlabel}}</h2>
                    <dl class="row">
                        {{#snapshot}}
                            <dt class="col-sm-4">{{label}}</dt>
                            <dd class="col-sm-8 enrol_apply-linebreaks">{{value}}</dd>
                        {{/snapshot}}
                    </dl>
                </div>
            {{/hassnapshot}}
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-5">
            <h2 class="h5">{{courselabel}}</h2>
            <p><a href="{{courseurl}}">{{coursename}}</a></p>
            {{#hascapacity}}
                <h2 class="h5">{{capacitylabel}}</h2>
                <dl class="row">
                    <dt class="col-6">{{placeslabel}}</dt>
                    <dd class="col-6">{{places}}</dd>
                    <dt class="col-6">{{applicantslabel}}</dt>
                    <dd class="col-6">{{applicants}}</dd>
                    <dt class="col-6">{{deferredlabel}}</dt>
                    <dd class="col-6">{{deferred}}</dd>
                </dl>
            {{/hascapacity}}
            {{#hashistory}}
                <h2 class="h5">{{historylabel}}</h2>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    {{#history}}
                        <li class="text-muted">{{applied}} &mdash; {{outcome}}</li>
                    {{/history}}
                </ul>
            {{/hashistory}}
        </div>
    </div>
    {{> enrol_apply/decision_controls }}
    {{{stickyfooter}}}
</form>
